  menuTitle: Two-Car House
  choices:
  - choiceName: Take both Cars
    carNumberMod: 0
    horseNumberMod: 0
    kidNumberMod: 0
    petNumberMod: 0
    homeHardeningMod: 0
    carSpeedMod: 1
    carLeaveTime: 2
    choiceDetail: Split up and take both cars during the evacuation.
    choiceThought: 
    choiceThoughtSprite: {fileID: 0}
    endGameFeedback: Some of the traffic congestion was caused by houses taking two
      cars. Maybe we can find a better way next time.
    isLocked: 0
    isNormal: 1
  - choiceName: Leave one Car
    carNumberMod: -1
    horseNumberMod: 0
    kidNumberMod: 0
    petNumberMod: 0
    homeHardeningMod: 0
    carSpeedMod: 1
    carLeaveTime: 1
    choiceDetail: Evacuate in one car, leaving the other car behind.
    choiceThought: 
    choiceThoughtSprite: {fileID: 0}
    endGameFeedback: "It\u2019s a good thing no one took two cars on the road, but
      residents are frustrated their cars were burned in their driveways."
    isLocked: 0
    isNormal: 1
  - choiceName: Relocate 2nd Car
    carNumberMod: -1
    horseNumberMod: 0
    kidNumberMod: 0
    petNumberMod: 0
    homeHardeningMod: 0
    carSpeedMod: 2
    carLeaveTime: 0
    choiceDetail: You know too many cars on the road cause traffic congestion, so
      you relocate your second car  on high risk days.
    choiceThought: 
    choiceThoughtSprite: {fileID: 0}
    endGameFeedback: 'An amazing community effort took place to reduce traffic congestion:
      people relocated their second cars before an evacuation notice! No doubt this
      act saved many lives.'
    isLocked: 1
    isNormal: 0
  longerTitle: Multi-Car Household
  descriptions:
  - 'Households with multiple cars face a dilemma during evacuations. Some wish to
    keep all their vehicles with them when they evacuate. It is very important to
    consider the consequences of such choices. Splitting the family into multiple
    vehicles during an evacuation increases risks of being separated, as well as
    causing additional congestion during evacuation. If it is important to keep both
    vehicles, consider relocating one of them to a safe place on red flag days to
    keep yourselves and your belongings safe. '
